hey everyone bandit here of all the fan  bases in the wide wide world of video  games the zelda fan base tends to stand  out for several reasons one of which is  the tendency for zelda fans to wonder  about what's not shown to them in the  video games this activity is also known  as theorizing for instance take link the  hero the the guy my dude sometimes he's  got a grandma sometimes he's got an  uncle sometimes a little sister but  where are his parents huh where are they  nintendo why is hyrule always changing  why is there only one breed of dog in  breath of the wild why are there no  female gorons choose one of these  questions mix in a couple of repeated  symbols across the fan base sprinkle in  some similar color schemes and garnish  it with a nice little touch of what they  said in the original japanese version of  the game and that's theorizing in a  nutshell  but to be honest with you it is a lot of  fun which is why i love doing it a lot  probably too much but anyway i know good  and well that the zelda youtube people  who are on the screen are not the only  types of fans that theorize about the  legend of zelda we all do on the screen  off the screen whatever which is why i  asked you about this the other day in  one of my community posts so i thought  it would be cool to talk about some of  your theories for a change to hear from  some of the zelda fanbase that isn't on  the screen and i picked five of the most  interesting in my opinion of course  theories from the comments section of  that one community post and we're gonna  be talking about them in this video last  little disclaimer here is please  remember that there are definitely some  like duplicates of theories in the  comments of that community post but i  will be crediting only the first  commenter that i saw to post said theory  oh and be sure to leave a like on this  video in support of us the fan base that  theorizes alright number one more people  reincarnate in hyrule than simply link  zelda and ganondorf this is a very  interesting theory because like lots of  things in the zelda universe it's just  kind of there and isn't really explained  people like impa who appears six  different times across eight different  zelda games or beetle who appears five  different times across six different  games are examples of this fact while  we're not presently able to answer this  mystery with any sort of confidence we  can definitely speculate and create our  own head canon which can be just as fun  in my opinion since beetle and impa  always come back as pretty much the same  individual and since we know that ghosts  and spirits exist in the land of hyrule  and of course since we already know that  the spirit of the hero reincarnates as  also pretty much the same individual  each time but without any memories of  his past lives i just assume that people  like beetle and impa kind of work the  same way whether orchestrated by the  goddesses or some other power what if  there was a spirit of the merchant or a  spirit of the defender who are the  spirits responsible for incarnating time  and time again as beetle and impa we may  never know the concrete answer to this  mystery for sure but until then this is  what i'm going with number two the  zora's evolution into the rito race was  not natural it was a product of divine  intervention okay so you know how the  rito who first appeared in the game wind  waker as the race of bird people who  live on dragon roost island evolved from  the zora who don't make a living  appearance in the game well after the  gods flooded the world with water to try  to stop ganon you know filling the world  with more water and less land have you  ever stopped to think about why that  would have forced fish people to evolve  into bird people if anything it may have  forced birds to evolve back into fish  since there was so much more water  everywhere and less land and trees for  birds to perch on however this theory  insinuates that because the gods flooded  hyrule to bury it beneath the sea along  with ganon and his monsters what if the  gods also forced the zora to evolve into  the rito so that the land underneath the  waves would remain untouched pretty  interesting isn't it also wouldn't that  kind of make hyrule atlantis  anyway moving on number three zelda has  to die to truly end the curse of the  demon tribe for those of you who are  familiar with the story of skyward sword  you know all too well that at the end of  the game demise aka the og demon king  can be seen cursing the descendants of  hylia aka all future zeldas and the  spirit of the hero aka all future links  with being visited by an incarnation of  demise's hatred for the rest of eternity  pretty harsh stuff i know but no matter  how you slice it according to demise's  own words zelda and link are the two  individuals who are cursed right quote  those like you those who share the blood  of the goddess and the spirit of the  hero they are eternally bound to this  curse right if you want to get technical  even the original japanese text  specifically states that quote you  people who possess the blood of the  goddess and the soul of the hero shall  forever be unable to escape from this  curse you people here you know what let  me write this in equation form i'm sorry  if this turns out looking horrible if  link plus zelda equals bad stuff then no  link and no zelda equals no bad stuff  makes sense right and sure demise  ultimately wants the triforce but he  didn't curse the triforce he cursed its  protectors link and zelda number four  are heart pieces or heart containers  considered canon this is kind of a funny  one because it's clearly meant to be a  piece of progressive gameplay i mean  obviously but it's a mystery that you  can't exactly dismiss either because  doing so would require you to dismiss  conversations and even entire characters  as non-canon from within the zelda games  like poking holes in the games like  swiss cheese  take the skull kids in the lost woods of  ocarina of time for instance after link  plays their songs back to them they  reward him with a piece of heart if  pieces of heart aren't canon and  therefore don't actually exist in zelda  lore then what else would they have  given him that we didn't get to see or  did this encounter even really happen in  the first place you would think it did  happen though since the skull kid from  majora's mask seems to remember link the  same question can be raised for the  pieces of heart rewarded from the  fishing hole or from the bomb chew  bowling alley or for bringing mama yu  yan her little puppy back do these  people or these encounters not actually  exist either and this debate is true for  all zelda games since pieces of heart  are kind of a staple of the series if  they aren't canon then i guess we just  need to get used to seeing stuff that  simply isn't real in these games but if  they are canon then that sparks an  entire other discussion about how link's  life works and why other people would  even have these things in the first  place but alas those are theories for  another day lastly does the mummified  ganondorf from the breath of the wild 2  trailer prove that breath of the wild  takes place in the fallen timeline and i  know that i said i took 5 theory ideas  from the comment section but  actually i only took four this one is  submitted by yours truly the gist of it  is that we know ganondorf was killed and  turned to stone in the adult timeline  right and in the child timeline was  stabbed through and completely killed as  well even though we don't actually know  what happened with old ganondorf's body  after twilight princess the fact remains  that he did actually die in that  timeline by way of a wound that should  permanently be visible on his body the  fallen timeline is the only one that  doesn't account for his physical body  only that he turned into the demon ganon  at some point prior to the events of a  link to the past if you look at the  ganondorf corpse in the breath of the  wild two trailers he definitely doesn't  look like he's made of stone and while  lots of people claim that the place the  green hand was holding him in the middle  of his chest is the same spot that he  was stabbed in in twilight princess ever  since we got the new trailer that shows  him standing up facing the camera if you  look at his chest there's no stab wound  where there should be one if this really  is the ganondorf from twilight princess  the only possibility left would be the  fallen timeline ganondorf whose body we  don't actually know what happened to  right and it is also true that according  to creating a champion the hylians don't  record the events of wind waker or  twilight princess as part of their  history they only record that ganondorf  became ganon and then reincarnated over  and over again this fits perfectly  within and only within the fallen  timeline where ganon was resurrected at  least four times with the fifth being  prevented as a result of the adventure  of link but of course since there are  many other factors in breath of the wild  that have made its timeline placement  notoriously debatable this remains just  my theory and that's the video did you  guys like these theories your theories  or did you think that they were way off  also would you like to see more videos  done in this format kind of as a give  and take from the community let me know  what you think in the comments below  also be sure to like this video if you  liked this video to get it spread around  to other zelda fans just like you and me  and subscribe to the channel if you  haven't already for much more nintendo  content to come as always humongous  thanks goes out to my bandit crew who  are the reason i'm able to do this kind  of content in the first place please say  hello to love hugh marcelo c brian t and  puzzle girl who all decided generously  to join the ranks of my elite if you  watching are interested in getting your  name up here with my crew and helping  these videos come to life please feel  free to check out that join button  located below any of my videos or follow  the links in the description to my  patreon and merge pages also down there  are the links to my social media pages  so come follow me on twitter or  instagram for all sorts of cool little  nuggets of whatever the heck i'm  thinking that's all i've got in this one  so as always i hope you have a wonderful  rest of your day this is bandit looking  forward to seeing you in the next one  and signing out  [Music]  you

